# Nuxt application test template
# Keep generated output, secrets and local machine state out of Git.
# Keep source directories, scenarios and test fixtures visible to version control.

# 1. Package managers and dependencies
**/node_modules/
**/.pnpm-store/
**/.pnp
**/.pnp.*
**/package-lock.json
**/yarn.lock
# pnpm-lock.yaml is canonical and must be committed.

# Package manager and runtime logs
**/npm-debug.log*
**/yarn-debug.log*
**/yarn-error.log*
**/pnpm-debug.log*
**/firebase-debug.log*
**/*.log

# 2. Local environment and credentials
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
!**/.env.*.example
**/service-account.json

# 3. OS and editor noise
**/Thumbs.db
**/.DS_Store
**/.AppleDouble
**/.Spotlight-V100/
**/.Trashes/
**/lost+found/
.idea/
.fleet/
.vscode/

# 4. Temporary files and editor backups
**/*.tmp
**/*.bak
**/*.swp
**/*.swo
**/*.orig
**/tmp/
**/temp/

# 5. Nuxt, Nitro, Vite and generated build artefacts
**/.cache/
**/.data/
**/.nuxi/
**/.nuxt/
**/.output/
**/.nitro/
**/.vite/
**/dist/
**/.netlify/
**/.vercel/
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/out-tsc/

# 6. Testing and documentation artefacts
**/.vitest/
**/coverage/
**/playwright-report/
**/test-results/
**/storybook-static/
**/cypress/screenshots/
**/cypress/videos/
**/docs/.vitepress/dist/
**/docs/.vitepress/cache/

# Do not ignore .storybook/ configuration, Nitro configuration,
# source data/, development/, storage/, sandbox/ or fixture directories.
